## Problem

The `Interner` is passed as `&mut Interner` throughout the compilation pipeline, blocking all parallelization:

```rust
// crates/rue-intern/src/lib.rs
pub fn intern(&mut self, s: &str) -> Symbol  // Takes &mut self!
```

This is the #1 blocker for parallel Sema (type checking).

## Current Threading

```
AstGen::new(&ast, &mut interner)  // &mut
    → Sema::new(rir, &mut interner, ...)  // &mut
        → analyze_function() repeatedly mutates interner
```

## Proposed Solutions

### Option A: Concurrent Interner (Recommended)

Use lock-free concurrent data structures:

```rust
use dashmap::DashMap;
use std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32;

pub struct ConcurrentInterner {
    map: DashMap<Box<str>, Symbol>,
    strings: parking_lot::RwLock<Vec<Box<str>>>,
    next_id: AtomicU32,
}

impl ConcurrentInterner {
    pub fn intern(&self, s: &str) -> Symbol {  // Takes &self!
        if let Some(sym) = self.map.get(s) {
            return *sym;
        }
        // Lock-free insert with CAS
        let sym = Symbol::from_raw(self.next_id.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed));
        self.map.entry(s.into()).or_insert(sym);
        sym
    }
}
```

### Option B: Pre-intern All Symbols

Collect all identifiers during parsing, intern them all before Sema:

```rust
// During AST construction, collect all identifier strings
let all_idents: HashSet<&str> = collect_all_identifiers(&ast);

// Intern them all upfront
for ident in all_idents {
    interner.intern(ident);
}

// Now Sema only needs &Interner (immutable)
```

### Option C: Use Existing Crate

- `lasso` - High-performance concurrent string interner (used by rustc)
- `string-interner` - Simple concurrent interner

## Impact

Unblocks:
- Parallel function type checking (Sema)
- Parallel CFG construction (if interner refs are needed)
- Future: parallel multi-file parsing

