## Goal

Design the `ParamArena` data structure that will store all function/method parameter data in a single contiguous allocation.

## Proposed Design

```rust
/// Central storage for all parameter data.
/// Uses indices for zero-copy references.
pub struct ParamArena {
    /// All parameter names (indexed by slot)
    param_names: Vec<Spur>,
    /// All parameter types (indexed by slot)
    param_types: Vec<Type>,
    /// All parameter modes (indexed by slot)
    param_modes: Vec<RirParamMode>,
}

/// A range into the ParamArena.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub struct ParamRange {
    start: u32,
    len: u32,
}

impl ParamArena {
    /// Allocate space for a function's parameters.
    /// Returns a range that can be stored in FunctionInfo.
    pub fn alloc_params(
        &mut self,
        types: impl Iterator<Item = Type>,
        modes: impl Iterator<Item = RirParamMode>,
    ) -> ParamRange;

    /// Allocate space for a method's parameters (includes names).
    pub fn alloc_method_params(
        &mut self,
        names: impl Iterator<Item = Spur>,
        types: impl Iterator<Item = Type>,
    ) -> ParamRange;

    /// Get parameter types for a range.
    pub fn get_types(&self, range: ParamRange) -> &[Type];

    /// Get parameter modes for a range.
    pub fn get_modes(&self, range: ParamRange) -> &[RirParamMode];

    /// Get parameter names for a range.
    pub fn get_names(&self, range: ParamRange) -> &[Spur];
}
```

## Design Decisions

1. **Separate vs unified storage**: Keep types/modes/names in separate Vecs for better cache locality when iterating just one
2. **Index type**: Use u32 (4GB of params is plenty)
3. **Allocation strategy**: Append-only during declaration gathering

